WB-300VB-IP-5: force CFI word writes on the parallel NOR.

The Macronix parallel NOR on this board's LPC32xx EMC hangs on CFI buffered
writes -- the buffered-program command sequence (0x25/0x29) never completes,
so `mtd write` (and therefore sysupgrade) hangs indefinitely. Single-word
programming (0xA0), which a userspace raw-CFI flasher proves works reliably on
this exact chip, is unaffected. cfi_cmdset_0002 exposes no Kconfig / DT / CFLAGS
lever for this -- FORCE_WORD_WRITE is a bare #define -- so patch it on. This is a
necessary hardware quirk for this target (single-NOR board; word writes are
always correct, only slightly slower).

--- a/drivers/mtd/chips/cfi_cmdset_0002.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/chips/cfi_cmdset_0002.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 #include <linux/mtd/xip.h>

 #define AMD_BOOTLOC_BUG
-#define FORCE_WORD_WRITE 0
+#define FORCE_WORD_WRITE 1

 #define MAX_RETRIES 3

